{"id": "EUVD-2026-50325", "enisaUuid": "67cc29f9-4fbf-3fa8-bc11-ee13b5fb842e", "description": "nanoid (Nano ID) before 5.1.6 contains an infinite loop in the customAlphabet and customRandom functions. When these functions are configured with a size of 0, the internal generation loop never satisfies its exit condition and spins indefinitely, hanging the calling thread. An application that passes an unvalidated, attacker-controlled size of 0 to these functions is exposed to a denial-of-service condition.", "datePublished": "2026-07-29T13:32:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:24:01", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ai/nanoid/releases/tag/5.1.6", "https://github.com/ai/nanoid/commit/cb3626d0f3342fdf179cd425fd9c4fbb92c7d0e7", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nanoid-before-infinite-loop-via-zero-size-in-customalphabet-and-customrandom"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-67213", "GHSA-2v37-7h3g-55p8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.59, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c31c7506-55d8-33c1-ac10-030e5e6292b9", "product": {"name": "nanoid", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.3.17"}, {"id": "fd2ff87b-a172-3238-8cd4-2503e7ab97bf", "product": {"name": "nanoid", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 <5.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0cb3817c-056b-300d-8584-9b8aecfa00c8", "vendor": {"name": "nanoid_project"}}], "isExploited": false}